homelab-webproxy (0.1.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a per-site `websocket: true` flag: proxies websocket Upgrade
    handshakes (proxy_http_version 1.1 + Upgrade/Connection headers) and
    streams the response (proxy_buffering off + 3600s timeouts). Fixes
    Plex's live/notifications/streaming behind the edge, which a plain
    proxy silently broke. apply-sites also drops an http-context
    `map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade` into conf.d whenever any site
    uses the flag. Non-websocket vhosts are unchanged.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:58:18 -0500

homelab-webproxy (0.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v0.1.9

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:18:00 -0500

homelab-webproxy (0.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pull model: a site may use discover: <feature> to derive its upstream
    pool live from homelab-api (fleet view); homelab-webproxy-pull.timer
    re-runs apply-sites every ~2min and reloads nginx only when a pool
    changes. Lets the roundcube pool track the fleet with no manual edit.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:17:58 -0500

